---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/average-restaurant-tip/" jsonLd={jsonLd} nav={nav}>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="guide-intro"><a href="/">Restaurant tip calculator</a> / Average restaurant tip</p>
    <h1>Average Restaurant Tip: What Most Americans Leave in 2026</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The short answer: <strong>15–20% of the pre-tax bill</strong>, with 20% now the default for full table service.
      Here's the data, the per-service breakdown, and the math — free, no sign-up.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Calculator mode="dinein" />

  <aside class="ad ad-leaderboard ad-below" aria-label="Advertisement">
    <p class="ad-label">Advertisement</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" id="ad-below" data-size="728 × 90 · 300 × 250">
      <!-- e.g. GAM slot: /XXXXXXX/rtc_avgptip_below-calc -->
    </div>
  </aside>

  <!-- ============ THE NUMBERS ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="average">
    <h2>What's the average tip percentage in U.S. restaurants?</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Industry point-of-sale data and consumer surveys agree: <strong>20% is the average restaurant tip</strong> for
        full table service, and the customary range has settled at <strong>15–20% of the pre-tax bill</strong>. In
        Toast's 2023 restaurant trends data, full-service tips averaged just under 20% while counter-service orders
        averaged in the mid-teens. A 2023 Pew Research survey found about <strong>three-quarters of Americans</strong>
        say tipping is expected of them at sit-down restaurants — and most tip around 20%.
      </p>
      <p>
        What that means in practice: 15% reads as "fine," 18% as "good," and <strong>20–25% as "great."</strong> The
        percentage for tipping has crept up over the past two decades — the old 15%-as-default norm has become a floor.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="guide-intro">Normal restaurant tip by level of service — the range to use:</p>
        <div class="menu">
          <div class="menu-row">
            <span class="menu-name">Counter service, coffee shops</span><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"
            ></span><span class="menu-val">0–10%, optional</span>
          </div>
          <div class="menu-row">
            <span class="menu-name">Buffet, full service</span><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
              class="menu-val">10–20%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="menu-row">
            <span class="menu-name">Table service, acceptable</span><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"
            ></span><span class="menu-val">15–18%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="menu-row">
            <span class="menu-name">Table service, good-to-great</span><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"
            ></span><span class="menu-val">20–25%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="menu-row">
            <span class="menu-name">Large groups (6+)</span><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
              class="menu-val">18–20% auto-added</span>
          </div>
          <div class="menu-row">
            <span class="menu-name">Bar drinks</span><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
              class="menu-val">$1–2 a drink, or 15–20%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <table class="worked">
          <caption>Average tip on common check sizes (18% vs 20%):</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Bill</th><th scope="col">18% tip</th><th scope="col">20% tip</th><th scope="col">Total @20%</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>$25.00</td><td>$4.50</td><td>$5.00</td><td>$30.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td>$40.00</td><td>$7.20</td><td>$8.00</td><td>$48.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td>$60.00</td><td>$10.80</td><td>$12.00</td><td>$72.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td>$100.00</td><td>$18.00</td><td>$20.00</td><td>$120.00</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="worked-note">
          Run any check through the <a href="#calculator">tip calculator above</a> — tip, total, and per-person split
          update live. Bill already has an auto-gratuity? Read up on the
          <a href="/service-charge-on-restaurant-bill/">service charge on your restaurant bill</a> first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHY TIPS ARE THE NORM ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="why">
    <h2>Why tips are the norm — and why the average keeps rising</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        U.S. federal law lets employers pay tipped staff as little as <strong>$2.13 an hour</strong>, with tips making
        up the difference to the regular minimum wage. Tips therefore aren't a bonus for servers — they're most of the
        paycheck. That's the root of the "always tip at sit-down restaurants" rule, and it's why the customary tip has
        drifted from 15% to 20%: restaurants raised expectations alongside menu prices, and payment screens nudged
        tipping into counter-service too.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're traveling, remember this is a U.S. norm. In much of Europe service is included in the price, and in
        Japan tipping is unnecessary — check local customs first. And if your server gets it wrong, knowing
        <a href="/how-much-tip-waitress-waiter/">how much to tip a waitress or waiter</a> per service level keeps the
        math painless.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="faq">
    <h2>Average tip questions, answered</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>What is the average restaurant tip in the U.S.?</summary>
        <p>
          Most U.S. diners tip between 15% and 20% of the pre-tax bill, and 20% has become the norm for full table
          service. Counter and fast-casual orders average under 10%, while full-service check averages land near
          19–20% in industry point-of-sale data (Toast, 2023).
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What percentage is customary for tipping in a restaurant?</summary>
        <p>
          The customary tip for restaurant table service is 15–20% of the pre-tax amount: 15–18% for adequate service
          and 20% or more for good-to-great service. Etiquette guides have quoted 18–20% for decades, and that same
          range is the standard restaurant tip today.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is 20% now the standard restaurant tip?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes — 20% is widely treated as the default for full-service table service in the U.S., with 18% seen as
          slightly conservative and 22–25% for exceptional service. A 2023 Pew Research survey found most Americans
          tip about 20% at sit-down restaurants.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What is a normal restaurant tip for average or bad service?</summary>
        <p>
          For average or merely acceptable service, 15–18% is normal. For poor service, diners commonly drop to 10%
          rather than zero — the tipped minimum wage is as low as $2.13 an hour, so zeroing the tip pulls money
          directly out of the server's pay. For clearly hostile service, speak to a manager instead of leaving nothing
          silently.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What is the average tip on a $50 restaurant bill?</summary>
        <p>
          At 18%, the tip on a $50 bill is $9.00 for a total of $59.00. At 20%, it is $10.00 for a total of $60.00.
          Split between two people, that is $29.50 or $30.00 each.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you tip before or after tax?</summary>
        <p>
          Etiquette says calculate the percentage on the pre-tax subtotal. Most people just tip on the after-tax total
          because it is the number at the bottom of the check — the difference is usually well under a dollar, so
          either approach is fine as long as you are consistent.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ SOURCES ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="sources">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/11/22/more-americans-are-saying-tipping-is-now-expected/">
          Pew Research Center — "More Americans Are Saying Tipping Is Now Expected" (Nov 2023)
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://pos.toasttab.com/resources/restaurant-trends-report">Toast POS Restaurant Trends Report (2023)</a>
        — average tip percentage by service type.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/minimum-wage/tips">U.S. Department of Labor — tipped minimum wage factsheet</a>
        ($2.13 federal tipped minimum wage, tip credit rules).
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <aside class="ad ad-native ad-inline" aria-label="Advertisement">
    <p class="ad-label">Advertisement</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" id="ad-native" data-size="Native banner · 280px reserved">
      <!-- Paste the native banner tag from your ad network here -->
    </div>
  </aside>

  <Related exclude="/average-restaurant-tip/" />
</Layout>